# Scheduling front-desk-ai with cron (Linux, and macOS if the machine stays awake).
#
# Install:  crontab -e     then paste the lines you want.
# Check:    crontab -l
# Logs:     tail -f {{REPO_PATH}}/data/logs/cron.log
#
# The jobs below are exactly what this command prints for this agent - one
# entry per job under `schedule:` in config/agent.yaml, with its own real
# command and cadence:
#
#     make schedule ARGS="--all"
#
# Re-run that command (and paste its output here) any time config/agent.yaml's
# schedule: block changes - do not hand-edit the cadences below and expect
# them to stay in sync. `make schedule` on its own (or with --command/
# --cadence) generates one snippet for any single command you name instead:
#
#     make schedule ARGS="--cadence every-15-min"
#     make schedule ARGS="--command 'tools/run.py --once' --cadence every-5-min"
#
# cron starts with almost no environment, so every path below MUST be
# absolute. Replace {{REPO_PATH}} with the output of `pwd` in this folder.

# job: triage  cadence: */5 * * * *  (from config/agent.yaml schedule.triage)
*/5 * * * * cd {{REPO_PATH}} && {{REPO_PATH}}/.venv/bin/python tools/run.py --once >> {{REPO_PATH}}/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# job: confirmations  cadence: */15 * * * *  (from config/agent.yaml schedule.confirmations)
*/15 * * * * cd {{REPO_PATH}} && {{REPO_PATH}}/.venv/bin/python tools/run.py --once --confirmations >> {{REPO_PATH}}/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# job: coach  cadence: 0 3 * * 1  (from config/agent.yaml schedule.coach)
0 3 * * 1 cd {{REPO_PATH}} && {{REPO_PATH}}/.venv/bin/python tools/coach.py analyze >> {{REPO_PATH}}/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Start in shadow mode. Only add a schedule after you have watched a few real
# passes by hand and worked the review queue.
